  "exact_diff_conclusion": {
    "payload": "The complete successor restores exactly to the authentic predecessor, including raw serialized YAML, after restoring the two original current note values and removing the single appended correction event. No other field or formatting change remains.",
    "current_notes_after": {
      "notes": "The TOGO M2854 source names calf blood, a blood material rather than serum; calf specifies developmental origin. The source does not explicitly say whole or establish defibrination, lysis, supplier or the basis of its literal 10% receiving dose. Those processing and percentage-basis details remain unknown. The known source material scope can be represented without inferring those details. Source labels retained as nonresolving provenance: [{\"case_id\": \"CM_NAME:556fc068943d632ce6e95108d337291521fc471fbc26165d3437068246f4e258\", \"raw_label\": \"calf blood\"}]. No global generic alias, supplier equivalence, role approval or complete publication approval is conferred. Receiving-medium dose and unit repairs remain separate. Existing native holds and rejected labels are preserved.",
      "ontology_mapping.evidence[0].notes": "The TOGO M2854 source names calf blood, a blood material rather than serum; calf specifies developmental origin. The source does not explicitly say whole or establish defibrination, lysis, supplier or the basis of its literal 10% receiving dose. Those processing and percentage-basis details remain unknown. The known source material scope can be represented without inferring those details. Broader material parent only; distinct local preparation identity remains."
    },
    "appended_history": {
      "timestamp": "2026-11-08T08:35:09.393695+00:00",
      "curator": "Codex worker10 /root",
      "action": "CORRECTED_CALF_BLOOD_EXPLANATION",
      "changes": "Issue #1237, W10-SV3-SKEPTIC-CALF-BLOOD-WORDING: corrected only current record and mapping-evidence notes. The source names calf blood, a blood material rather than serum; calf describes developmental origin, not the blood-versus-serum distinction. Removed the assertion that the source explicitly identifies whole blood. It states a literal 10% receiving dose without establishing its basis. Original history remains verbatim. Identifier, broader blood mapping, LLM_SUGGESTION provenance, source-specific applicability, unknown processing and percentage basis, nonresolving generic label and all role/export holds remain unchanged. No product, fraction-processing protocol, alias or identity change is inferred. Filed finding: https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6719103915",
      "previous_status": "MAPPED",
      "new_status": "MAPPED",
      "llm_assisted": true
    },
    "original_history": "Both prior events, including the historically erroneous CREATED explanation and subsequent issue1226 provenance correction, are retained verbatim. The new event explicitly corrects the active explanation without rewriting history.",
